Hi All,

I'd like to fit a gamma-Poisson distribution to account for over dispersion in count data using INLA.

In its simplest form the model in the JAGS dialect of the BUGS language is as below:

 model{
 bIntercept ~ dnorm(0, 5^-2)
  for(i in 1:length(Count)) {
    log(eCount[i)] <- bIntercept

    eDispersion[ii] ~ dgamma(1 / sDispersion^2, 1 / sDispersion^2)

    Count[i] ~ dpois(eCount[ii] * eDispersion[ii])
  }
}

The key feature is that the alpha = beta in the gamma distribution so that it has an expectation of 1.

Any help or guidance would be greatly appreciated

Joe

