Dear Håvard,

Thank you for the prompt reply. Before pulling together the small example, I was wondering whether INLA's implementation of the hurdle model is different than implementing the two stages of the model separately.
That is,
1) Convert the original response variable to binary (0 = zero observations, 1 = non-zero observations) and use INLA to run the logistic regression component of the hurdle model
2) Convert 0s in the original response variable to NA and use INLA to run the gamma likelihood component of the model

If the appropriate settings are the same, should the results be the same as that in the hurdle model? Is there a benefit to implementing the two models in the hurdle structure in INLA?

Thank you!
Elizabeth

